<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Sidecar bundling (Phase 1 onward): the embedded Python 3.12 + venv
    at Contents/Resources/rapid-mlx/ ships dynamic libraries (mlx.so,
    tokenizers.so, etc.) that load their own .dylibs from inside the
    bundle. Apple's hardened runtime rejects this by default.

    Both keys are flagged informationally (not as errors) in the notary
    report. Same shape as Anaconda Navigator, Briefcase apps, framework
    MacPython distributions.
    -->

    <!--
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit: required by mlx's Metal JIT cache
    (~/Library/Caches/mlx) which compiles per-model shaders at runtime.
    Without this entitlement the runtime kills mlx-lm on first model
    load.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: required so the
    bundled python3.12 can load third-party .dylibs (e.g. tokenizers'
    Rust runtime, mlx's Metal runtime) without each one being signed
    by Apple or the same Team ID as the host.

    Empirically required — first Phase 2 spike codesign sweep WITHOUT
    this entitlement broke dlopen for every wheel .so with "different
    Team IDs" error. Wheel .so's ship TeamIdentifier=not set; hardened
    runtime enforces library validation by default.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory: required
    by mlx's Metal command-buffer scheduler which writes shader code
    into JIT pages before execution. Discovered empirically during
    Phase 2 spike — without this, mlx Device(gpu, 0) initialisation
    succeeds but the first matmul SIGKILLs the runtime.

    Companion to allow-jit: JIT *compiles* the shaders (allow-jit),
    the executable-memory entitlement lets the result actually run.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
    com.apple.security.device.audio-input: required for Speech to Text
    dictation (DictationRecorder's AVAudioEngine capture). A hardened-
    runtime process WITHOUT this key is refused microphone access
    silently: AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess(for: .audio) returns false
    with no consent prompt and no TCC record, so the Audio tab's
    "Allow…" button appears dead. Debug builds are not hardened and
    prompt fine, which is why only the notarized release artifact was
    affected (#2134, shipped broken in 0.12.16).
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
